# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# This file must live at the git repository root. EAS builds its archive by
# copying the repository from the root down and reads .easignore only from here,
# even though eas.json is in app/. Without it EAS applies only this directory's
# .gitignore (just .vscode/), never app/.gitignore, which is how android/ and
# node_modules/ ended up in a 984 MB archive.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the archive rather than adding to it, so
# everything that must stay out is listed here, including what the .gitignore
# files already cover. Paths are relative to the repository root.

# Editor config (root .gitignore).
.vscode/

# Installed on the build server from the lockfile.
node_modules/

# Generated by prebuild. Uploading it is actively harmful: EAS treats a project
# that already has android/ as bare and skips prebuild, so it would build this
# stale local tree instead of generating one from app.json and the config plugins.
app/android/
app/ios/

# Local native module build output. app/modules/ itself is source and must ship:
# autolinking reads it and the usage-stats module lives there.
app/modules/*/android/build/
app/modules/*/android/.cxx/
app/modules/*/android/.gradle/

# Local tooling and caches.
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.kotlin/
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo
.claude/

# Not part of the app build.
docs/
chats/
app/store/screenshots/

# Never upload signing material. EAS stores the keystore server-side; a stray
# copy in the archive would be one more place for it to leak from.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.pem

# Local env and logs.
.env*.local
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
